# Applied by the Cloudflare Worker only. GitHub Pages does not read this file.
#
# A full Content-Security-Policy is not set here. Several pages already send
# their own CSP in a meta tag, and a response header is enforced as well as
# that meta policy. One site-wide policy would break the darts pages that load
# Tailwind, React, and Babel from CDNs, and the camera prototype. Those pages
# keep the CSP they already declare.
#
# frame-ancestors is ignored inside a meta tag, so clickjacking protection is
# set here. Strict-Transport-Security is left to the Cloudflare dashboard:
# includeSubDomains / preload is unsafe until every hostname is HTTPS.

/*
	X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
	Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
	X-Frame-Options: DENY
	Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
	Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
